  "wikitext": "{{PageDisplay}}\n[[File:Stone Block.png|200px|left|Stone blocks]]\n{{Infobox\n |title = [[Supplies|Supply]]\n |level = 34\n |price = 1 to 342\n |upgrades = {{Infoicon|grocerys|big|link=[[Grocery Store]]}}  {{Infoicon|gifts|big|link=Gift Shop}} {{Infoicon|spa|big|link=Spa}} {{Infoicon|townh|big|link=Town Hall}}\n |base = 95\n |dia = 10\n}}\n'''Stone blocks''' are [[supplies]] used to upgrade the [[Grocery Store|grocery store]], the [[Gift Shop|gift shop]], the [[spa]] and the [[Town Hall]].\n\nThey are unlocked at [[experience]] level 34.\n\nThey are stored in the [[barn]].\n{{Clr}}\n----\n==='''Getting stone blocks'''===\nA sure way to get a stone block is to buy it with 10 {{Infoicon|dia}}.\n\nStone blocks can also sometimes be found in [[Roadside Shop|roadside shops]] for 1 to 342 {{Infoicon|coin}} per unit.\n\nFinally, stone blocks can be randomly obtained when players:\n* open [[Mystery Box|mystery boxes]] and [[Catalogue|mystery packages]]\n* spin the [[Wheel of Fortune]]\n* fully satisfy a [[Town Visitors|town visitor]]\n* win prizes in [[Derby|derbies]]\n* use [[Mystery Net|mystery nets]] in the [[Fishing Lake|fishing lake]]\n* watch a Night at the Movies [[trailer]]\n----\n{{Navigation}}\n{{Languages\n|de = Steinblock\n|es = Bloques de piedra\n|fr = Pierre de taille\n|it = Blocco Di Pietra\n|no = Stein\n}}\n[[Category:Supplies]]",
  "wikitextHash": "fe76e40a1ee0adcc33aa0f16e92ae3d96c641e26defe47c5f06cb804c1432651"
